  "script": "A beast with four doors that can hit sixty in just 3.5 seconds. That's the Audi RS6 Avant. After an outcry from fans, Audi brought the RS6 Avant to the U.S. in 2020, making it an instant hit. Under the hood is a 4.0-liter twin-turbocharged V8 pumping out 591 horsepower and 590 lb-ft of torque. The engine's exhilarating output makes it a standout in its class. Inside, luxury meets technology with features like the Bang & Olufsen sound system and Audi's Virtual Cockpit. Power is sent to all four wheels through an 8-speed automatic and Audi's Quattro system, mastering any road. This system enhances handling in all weather conditions. Originally priced around $120K, they go for about $130K today, reflecting a rare appreciation in value. So, is the RS6 Avant the most practical speed machine you could daily, or is it a bit too much?",
